module nvd-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcp6.{ frcp6-nevada }

// The District of Nevada's own periods, computed under the federal rules
// (FRCP 6(a) governs "any local rule"). Most apply "unless the court orders
// otherwise" where the rule says so; an extension request must meet LR IA
// 6-1, and one to extend a discovery-plan date also LR 26-3. Rules that
// state no period or limit stay out, as do these: the scheduling order
// within 30 days of the discovery plan or of the first defendant's answer
// (LR 16-1(a), (b)) and the early neutral evaluation session within 90 days
// after the first responding party appears (LR 16-6(d)), which bind the
// court; the 180 days of discovery measured from the first defendant's
// appearance past which a discovery plan needs special scheduling review
// (LR 26-1(b)(1)), a review threshold and not a deadline; the 270 days
// without a proceeding of record after which an action may be dismissed for
// want of prosecution (LR 41-1), a court power and not a party's deadline;
// the suspended joint pretrial order until 30 days after decision on the
// dispositive motions (LR 26-1(b)(5)), which runs from the court's
// decision; the clerk's custody of exhibits (LR 79-1(c)); the motion for
// attorney's fees, whose time is FRCP 54(d)(2)(B)'s and lit/frcp's (LR
// 54-14 sets its content only); the motion for reconsideration of an
// interlocutory order "within a reasonable time" (LR 59-1(c)); and the
// Local Patent Rules (Part III), which are out of scope. LR 7.1-1 (the
// disclosure statement with a party's first appearance) states no period.
// No fee is stated. The earlier D. Nev. outline's FRCP flow and its Supreme
// Court decisions (Twombly, Iqbal, Celotex, Anderson v. Liberty Lobby,
// Reeves, Catlin, Bowles, Hamer) are FRCP and FRAP authority and belong to
// lit/frcp and lit/frap; its Ninth Circuit decisions (Eitel v. McCool;
// Lopez v. Smith) are removed: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A motion for summary judgment or a response to one, its statement of
/// facts included (LR 56-1): at most 30 pages, excluding exhibits (LR
/// 7-3(a)).
limit summary-judgment-brief { pages <= 30 cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(a)" } cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(a)"
/// A reply in support of a motion for summary judgment: at most 20 pages
/// (LR 7-3(a)).
limit summary-judgment-reply { pages <= 20 cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(a)" } cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(a)"
/// Any other motion or response to a motion, and a pretrial or post-trial
/// brief, the motion and its points and authorities combined in one
/// document (LR 7-2(a)): at most 24 pages, excluding exhibits (LR 7-3(b)).
/// Objections to a magistrate judge's order or findings and
/// recommendations, and responses to them, are subject to the same limits
/// (LR IB 3-1(a), 3-2(a)).
limit motion-brief { pages <= 24 cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(b)" } cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(b)"
/// Any other reply: at most 12 pages, excluding exhibits (LR 7-3(b)).
limit reply-brief { pages <= 12 cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(b)" } cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(b)"
/// A motion to exceed the page limits, filed before the motion or brief is
/// due with a declaration of the reasons for and number of the additional
/// pages: at most three pages (LR 7-3(c)).
limit page-limit-motion { pages <= 3 cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(c)" } cite "D. Nev. LR 7-3(c)"

/// A motion for summary judgment is served (LR 7-2(b)).
event SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() paper summary-judgment-brief
/// A response to a motion for summary judgment is served (LR 7-2(b)).
event SummaryJudgmentResponseServed() paper summary-judgment-brief
/// Any other motion is served (LR 7-2(b)).
event MotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// A response to any other motion is served (LR 7-2(b)).
event ResponseServed() paper motion-brief
/// The prevailing party serves a proposed order for approval as to form
/// (LR 7-2(f)).
event ProposedOrderServed()
/// An opposing party is served with notice that the prevailing party filed
/// its proposed order (LR 7-2(f)).
event ProposedOrderFilingNoticed()
/// Trial is set to begin (LR 16-3(a)).
event TrialBegins()
/// A motion in limine is served (LR 16-3(a)).
event LimineMotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// An order scheduling the early neutral evaluation session is entered (LR
/// 16-6(c)).
event EvaluationSessionOrderEntered()
/// A motion for exemption from the Early Neutral Evaluation Program is
/// served (LR 16-6(c)).
event EvaluationExemptionMotionServed() paper motion-brief
/// The early neutral evaluation session is set to be held (LR 16-6(f)).
event EvaluationSessionHeld()
/// The first defendant answers or otherwise appears (LR 22-1, 26-1(a),
/// 26-2).
event FirstDefendantAppeared()
/// The parties hold the FRCP 26(f) conference (LR 26-1(a)).
event RuleTwentySixFConferenceHeld()
/// The close of discovery set by the discovery plan (LR 26-1(b)).
event DiscoveryCutoff()
/// The initial disclosure of experts under FRCP 26(a)(2) is made (LR
/// 26-1(b)(3)).
event ExpertDisclosureMade()
/// The deadline for dispositive motions set by the discovery plan passes
/// (LR 26-1(b)(5)).
event DispositiveMotionDeadline()
/// A deadline set in a discovery plan expires (LR 26-3).
event DiscoveryPlanDeadline()
/// A court proceeding at which an interpreter will be used is held (LR
/// 43-1).
event InterpretedProceedingHeld()
/// The judgment or decree under which costs are claimed is entered (LR
/// 54-1(a)).
event JudgmentEntered()
/// A bill of costs is served (LR 54-1(c)).
event CostBillServed()
/// An objection to a bill of costs is served (LR 54-1(c)).
event CostObjectionServed()
/// A party receives notice of the clerk's taxation of costs under LR
/// 54-1(f) (LR 54-12(a)).
event CostsTaxationNoticed()
/// The hearing on appointment of a receiver is held (LR 66-2).
event ReceiverHearingHeld()
/// A permanent receiver is appointed (LR 66-4(b)).
event PermanentReceiverAppointed()
/// A hearing on a receiver's further report or on a petition listed in LR
/// 66-5 is held (LR 66-5).
event ReceivershipHearingHeld()
/// A party withdraws an exhibit it produced (LR 79-1(d)).
event ExhibitWithdrawn()
/// The clerk notifies the parties to claim their exhibits (LR 79-1(e)).
event ExhibitClaimNoticed()
/// An attorney's motion to withdraw is filed (LR IA 11-6(b)).
event WithdrawalMotionFiled()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's order on a pretrial matter
/// (LR IB 3-1(a)).
event MagistrateOrderServed()
/// A party is served with a magistrate judge's findings and
/// recommendations (LR IB 3-2(a)).
event MagistrateFindingsServed()
/// A party is served with objections to a magistrate judge's order or
/// findings and recommendations (LR IB 3-1(a), 3-2(a)).
event MagistrateObjectionServed() paper motion-brief

/// LR 7-2(b): the deadline to file and serve points and authorities in
/// response to a motion for summary judgment is 21 days after service of
/// the motion; the time to file the motion itself is FRCP 56(b)'s. A
/// failure to respond is not consent to the motion (LR 7-2(d)).
deadline summary-judgment-response-period: 21.days after SummaryJudgmentMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 7-2(b): the deadline to file and serve a reply in support of a
/// motion for summary judgment is 14 days after service of the response.
deadline summary-judgment-reply-period: 14.days after SummaryJudgmentResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 7-2(b): for any other motion, the deadline to file and serve points
/// and authorities in response is 14 days after service of the motion. A
/// failure to respond, except to a motion for attorney's fees, is consent
/// to the granting of the motion (LR 7-2(d)).
deadline response-period: 14.days after MotionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 7-2(b): the deadline to file and serve a reply in support of any
/// other motion is seven days after service of the response. Surreplies
/// need leave of court.
deadline reply-period: 7.days after ResponseServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 7-2(f): the opposing parties have three days after service of a
/// proposed order to notify the prevailing party of any reason for
/// disapproval; failing that, they are deemed to approve it.
deadline proposed-order-disapproval-period: 3.days after ProposedOrderServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 7-2(f): an opposing party that timely served reasons for disapproval
/// may file a competing proposed order within three days of being served
/// with notice that the prevailing party filed its proposed order.
deadline competing-proposed-order-period: 3.days after ProposedOrderFilingNoticed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 7-2(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 16-3(a): unless the court orders otherwise, motions in limine are
/// filed 30 days before trial.
deadline limine-motion-period: 30.days before TrialBegins() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 16-3(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 16-3(a): responses to a motion in limine are filed and served no
/// later than 14 days after service of the motion; replies only with leave.
deadline limine-response-period: 14.days after LimineMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 16-3(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 16-6(c): in an employment-discrimination action, a motion for
/// exemption from the Early Neutral Evaluation Program is filed no later
/// than seven days after entry of the order scheduling the session.
deadline evaluation-exemption-motion-period: 7.days after EvaluationSessionOrderEntered() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 16-6(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 16-6(c): a response to the motion for exemption is filed within 14
/// days after service of the motion; no reply is allowed.
deadline evaluation-exemption-response-period: 14.days after EvaluationExemptionMotionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 16-6(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 16-6(f): the parties submit their written evaluation statements to
/// the evaluating magistrate judge's chambers by 4:00 p.m. seven days
/// before the session; they are not filed or served.
deadline evaluation-statement-period: 7.days before EvaluationSessionHeld() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 16-6(f)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 22-1: in an interpleader action, the plaintiff moves for a
/// scheduling conference within 30 days after the first defendant answers
/// or otherwise appears; LR 26-1(a) and (b) do not apply (LR 26-1(d)).
deadline interpleader-conference-motion-period: 30.days after FirstDefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 22-1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(a): the plaintiff initiates the scheduling of the FRCP 26(f)
/// conference, to be held within 30 days after the first defendant answers
/// or otherwise appears.
deadline discovery-conference-period: 30.days after FirstDefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(a): fourteen days after the FRCP 26(f) conference, the parties
/// submit a stipulated discovery plan and scheduling order.
deadline discovery-plan-period: 14.days after RuleTwentySixFConferenceHeld() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(b)(2): unless the discovery plan otherwise provides and the
/// court so orders, motions to amend the pleadings or to add parties are
/// filed 90 days before the close of discovery.
deadline amendment-motion-period: 90.days before DiscoveryCutoff() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(b)(3): unless the discovery plan otherwise provides and the
/// court so orders, expert disclosures under FRCP 26(a)(2) are made 60
/// days before the discovery cut-off date, modifying FRCP 26(a)(2)(D).
deadline expert-disclosure-period: 60.days before DiscoveryCutoff() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(b)(3): rebuttal-expert disclosures are made 30 days after the
/// initial disclosure of experts.
deadline rebuttal-expert-disclosure-period: 30.days after ExpertDisclosureMade() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(b)(4): unless the discovery plan otherwise provides and the
/// court so orders, dispositive motions are filed 30 days after the
/// discovery cut-off date.
deadline dispositive-motion-period: 30.days after DiscoveryCutoff() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-1(b)(5): unless the discovery plan otherwise provides and the
/// court so orders, the joint pretrial order is due 30 days after the
/// dispositive-motion deadline; if dispositive motions are filed, it is
/// suspended until 30 days after their decision or further order.
deadline joint-pretrial-order-period: 30.days after DispositiveMotionDeadline() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-1(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-2: unless the court orders otherwise, where no discovery plan is
/// required, discovery is completed within 180 days from the time the first
/// defendant answers or otherwise appears.
deadline discovery-without-plan-period: 180.days after FirstDefendantAppeared() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 26-3: a motion or stipulation to extend a deadline set in a discovery
/// plan must be received by the court no later than 21 days before the
/// deadline expires; a later request needs good cause, and one after it
/// expires also excusable neglect.
deadline discovery-extension-request-period: 21.days before DiscoveryPlanDeadline() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 26-3"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 43-1: a party who anticipates needing an interpreter files a written
/// notice at least 14 days before the proceeding; a party needing an
/// American Sign Language interpreter contacts the courtroom administrator
/// at least 14 days before it.
deadline interpreter-notice-period: 14.days before InterpretedProceedingHeld() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 43-1"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 54-1(a): a prevailing party who claims costs files and serves a bill
/// of costs and disbursements on the clerk's form no later than 14 days
/// after entry of the judgment or decree.
deadline cost-bill-period: 14.days after JudgmentEntered() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 54-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 54-1(c): the deadline to file and serve an objection to a bill of
/// costs is 14 days after its service; failing to object may be consent to
/// all the costs (LR 54-1(d)).
deadline cost-objection-period: 14.days after CostBillServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 54-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 54-1(c): the deadline to file and serve a response to an objection is
/// seven days after service of the objection.
deadline cost-objection-response-period: 7.days after CostObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 54-1(c)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 54-12(a): a motion to re-tax costs under FRCP 54(d), with points and
/// authorities, is filed and served within seven days after receipt of the
/// notice of the clerk's taxation under LR 54-1(f).
deadline retax-motion-period: 7.days after CostsTaxationNoticed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 54-12(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 66-2: a receiver is not appointed except after a hearing preceded by
/// at least 14 days' notice to the party sought to be subjected to
/// receivership and to all known creditors; a temporary receiver may be
/// appointed without notice under FRCP 65(b).
deadline receiver-notice-period: 14.days before ReceiverHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 66-2"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 66-4(b): within 60 days of being appointed, a permanent receiver files
/// a verified report and account of the administration, heard on 14 days'
/// notice to all parties and known creditors.
deadline receiver-report-period: 60.days after PermanentReceiverAppointed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 66-4(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 66-5: unless the court orders otherwise, the receiver gives all
/// interested parties and creditors at least 14 days' notice of the hearing
/// of its further reports and of the petitions the rule lists.
deadline receivership-hearing-notice-period: 14.days before ReceivershipHearingHeld() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 66-5"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 79-1(d): if no appeal is taken, after final judgment and the time for
/// a notice of appeal and a new-trial motion have passed, a party may
/// withdraw an exhibit it produced on 21 days' prior written notice to all
/// parties.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-notice-period: 21.days before ExhibitWithdrawn() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 79-1(d)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR 79-1(e): exhibits not withdrawn within 21 days after the clerk
/// notifies the parties to claim them are destroyed or disposed of as the
/// court orders.
deadline exhibit-claim-period: 21.days after ExhibitClaimNoticed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR 79-1(e)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR IA 11-6(b): unless the court orders otherwise, the affected client
/// may file a response to its attorney's motion to withdraw within 14 days
/// of the filing of the motion.
deadline withdrawal-response-period: 14.days after WithdrawalMotionFiled() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR IA 11-6(b)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR IB 3-1(a): the deadline to file and serve specific written
/// objections to a magistrate judge's order on a pretrial matter is 14 days
/// after service of the order.
deadline magistrate-order-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateOrderServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR IB 3-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR IB 3-2(a): the deadline to file and serve specific written
/// objections, with points and authorities, to a magistrate judge's
/// findings and recommendations is 14 days after their service.
deadline magistrate-findings-objection-period: 14.days after MagistrateFindingsServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR IB 3-2(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}

/// LR IB 3-1(a), 3-2(a): the deadline to file and serve a response to
/// objections is 14 days after service of the objection; replies only with
/// leave of court.
deadline magistrate-objection-response-period: 14.days after MagistrateObjectionServed() counted_by frcp6-nevada cite "D. Nev. LR IB 3-1(a)"
{
  forum frcp
}
